WEBVTT

00:00.670 --> 00:02.980
The Pokémon Elections 720!

00:03.910 --> 00:07.020
These Pokémon Elections will determine the Pokémon that will be given away during the movie!

00:08.090 --> 00:11.540
We will now start taking your votes via the data broadcast!

00:12.900 --> 00:16.290
Push the d-button on your remote control and vote for the Pokémon you want!

00:16.890 --> 00:18.740
All right, the anime starts now!

00:22.000 --> 00:31.840
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:32.880 --> 00:33.680
This is good stuff.

00:36.230 --> 00:40.190
Must have been an eccentric person to make offerings in a place like this.

00:40.570 --> 00:41.680
You're wrong.

00:43.370 --> 00:46.020
These are offerings for <i>us</i>.

01:02.420 --> 01:04.570
Wh-Who's there?!

01:04.960 --> 01:06.900
We won't be angry at you, so show yourselves!

01:13.680 --> 01:15.020
What are those guys?

01:16.020 --> 01:17.010
Let's see...

01:17.380 --> 01:18.860
They're called Bokurei.

01:21.840 --> 01:23.510
What are they saying, Nyarth?

01:24.100 --> 01:28.060
They're saying, "You're eating our sweets, that's so mean!"

01:28.500 --> 01:30.870
Do they have "They're ours" written anywhere or what?

01:31.140 --> 01:35.070
Hmph! We found them, so they're ours!

01:36.990 --> 01:37.150
Hey!

01:39.670 --> 01:41.370
Don't be so stingy!

01:46.500 --> 01:47.690
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wha?!

01:48.240 --> 01:50.470
What's up with these branches?! They're creeping me out!

01:51.600 --> 01:52.360
Let go!

01:52.800 --> 01:55.810
This is no way to treat someone over some sweets!

01:57.460 --> 01:59.480
If that's how you're gonna act, I'll just eat more of them!

01:59.650 --> 02:02.070
What belongs to Bokurei belongs to me!

02:08.930 --> 02:10.010
Let go!

02:12.930 --> 02:13.350
Let go!

02:14.060 --> 02:16.230
This is mine!

02:16.230 --> 02:17.510
Mine...!

02:30.160 --> 02:30.730
Let's do this!

02:31.600 --> 02:34.850
Let's get some training for the Gym match at the Eisetsu Gym done today as well!

02:44.460 --> 02:44.820
Hey...

02:45.240 --> 02:46.400
Something's falling...

02:48.560 --> 02:49.310
Satoshi!

02:53.490 --> 02:55.530
Wh-What's this...?

02:59.290 --> 03:05.010
The Forest's Curse and the White Bokurei!

03:05.530 --> 03:12.190
As Satoshi and his friends continue their journey to the Eisetsu Gym, they encounter a Bokurei at the foot of a mountain.

03:12.560 --> 03:14.120
Satoshi, are you all right?

03:14.480 --> 03:15.040
Yeah...

03:18.730 --> 03:20.570
I wonder if it fell down from a tree...

03:21.040 --> 03:23.770
It fell from the sky! The sky! Eureka saw it!

03:23.920 --> 03:25.190
From the sky, huh?

03:26.970 --> 03:28.750
Bokurei, the Stump Pokémon.

03:28.980 --> 03:35.230
It is said that these Pokémon are created when spirits possess rotten tree stumps. They prefer to live in abandoned forests.

03:36.410 --> 03:38.190
It has a different color than the one in the Zukan.

03:38.470 --> 03:41.050
It is alternate-colored. How rare!

03:41.390 --> 03:42.800
Whoa, so cute!

03:43.740 --> 03:45.240
Nice to meet you, Bokurei.

03:56.970 --> 03:58.060
Is this a move it's using?

03:58.460 --> 03:59.480
It is Forest's Curse!

04:01.050 --> 04:02.790
Hey, wait!

04:03.300 --> 04:04.970
Pikachu, Iron Tail!

04:08.100 --> 04:09.490
Well done, Pikachu!

04:11.810 --> 04:13.030
I wonder what that was about.

04:15.150 --> 04:17.910
It lives in abandoned forests, correct?

04:18.430 --> 04:21.870
Is it not a little unusual for it to come down to the foot of a mountain like this?

04:22.160 --> 04:25.630
Apparently they turn big trees into their habitat and imitate children's voices.

04:26.140 --> 04:29.590
Using these voices, they lure people into the forest and cause them to get lost.

04:29.840 --> 04:31.330
That's what the legend says.

04:31.610 --> 04:35.070
Sounds fun! Eureka wants to hear those voices too!

04:36.060 --> 04:40.530
Well, I don't. I don't want to get lost in a forest, after all!

04:40.530 --> 04:42.410
I do not want this either! Never!

04:44.970 --> 04:45.880
I'm hungry...

04:49.420 --> 04:51.000
I've got English muffins; do you want some?

04:51.270 --> 04:52.510
Yeah, sure!

04:52.750 --> 04:54.170
Thank you, Serena!

04:56.350 --> 04:57.450
Thanks for the...

04:59.660 --> 05:00.860
A ghost!

05:00.860 --> 05:03.150
Hey you! That's mine!

05:05.580 --> 05:07.970
This little one likes sweets, I'm sure of it!

05:08.460 --> 05:09.970
Serena, have you got more?

05:10.640 --> 05:11.590
Y-Yeah...

05:13.000 --> 05:14.090
Here.

05:15.080 --> 05:16.040
Wanna eat this?

05:20.660 --> 05:22.110
Hey, where are your friends?

05:24.140 --> 05:24.860
Are you alone?

05:25.220 --> 05:25.980
Aren't there any others of you?

05:29.160 --> 05:31.530
Could it be lost?

05:31.530 --> 05:33.060
In that case, let's take it back...

05:33.660 --> 05:34.640
...to wherever its friends are.

05:35.210 --> 05:36.940
Take it back? But how?

05:37.690 --> 05:40.700
Serena, check if there are any big trees in this area.

05:41.290 --> 05:41.790
Oh!

05:42.250 --> 05:43.200
Give me a second.

05:44.380 --> 05:46.060
Looks like there's one at the top of this mountain.

05:47.810 --> 05:48.020
This is...

05:49.080 --> 05:54.010
It says that long ago, many people heard children's voices and got lost there.

05:54.530 --> 05:57.930
So when they set up a small shrine and started bringing offerings,

05:58.350 --> 06:01.500
the voices disappeared and no one got lost any more.

06:02.060 --> 06:04.210
This practice continues to this day, it seems.

06:06.170 --> 06:07.180
Bingo!

06:07.630 --> 06:09.710
All right, let's go to the top!

06:11.700 --> 06:12.410
Let's go together.

06:12.930 --> 06:14.330
We'll bring you home.

06:23.510 --> 06:24.000
What's the matter?

06:33.330 --> 06:34.500
It's a Digda.

06:43.130 --> 06:43.940
Don't worry.

06:44.410 --> 06:46.660
There's no need to be afraid of the Digda and the Dugtrio.

06:47.010 --> 06:48.610
They're saying hello to us.

06:57.520 --> 07:01.640
This might be the first time this Bokurei has seen a Digda and a Dugtrio.

07:01.870 --> 07:02.900
The first time?

07:02.900 --> 07:05.270
I am sure this is also the first time it has left its habitat.

07:11.030 --> 07:14.480
So that's why this little one got startled when it saw us.

07:15.310 --> 07:15.850
Bokurei...

07:16.410 --> 07:22.850
The outside world is completely unfamiliar to you, but it's full of different Pokémon: Fun guys, nice guys... All kinds of guys!

07:23.360 --> 07:26.540
Let's meet lots of Pokémon and make lots of friends!

07:26.770 --> 07:27.040
Okay?

07:33.640 --> 07:34.740
Wait!

07:34.740 --> 07:35.980
Don't rush!

07:41.880 --> 07:43.940
Whoa!

07:45.030 --> 07:46.550
That's a great view.

07:49.610 --> 07:50.860
The air is fresh too.

07:52.800 --> 07:54.980
Shall we take a break around here?

07:54.980 --> 07:55.590
Yeah, let's.

07:56.160 --> 07:56.880
Okay!

07:58.190 --> 08:00.340
Squishy, you take a sunbath.

08:07.180 --> 08:08.310
Let's have a snack.

08:08.650 --> 08:10.350
I've made macarons too!

08:10.350 --> 08:10.970
Wahey!

08:13.490 --> 08:14.640
Ta-da!

08:14.640 --> 08:15.270
Here you go!

08:16.550 --> 08:17.410
They look yummy!

08:23.250 --> 08:24.500
Harimaron!

08:44.380 --> 08:45.090
What's the matter?

08:45.420 --> 08:46.350
They're macarons.

08:46.880 --> 08:47.770
You like them, right?

08:49.610 --> 08:51.670
Stop, stop! Calm down.

08:53.890 --> 08:55.600
There, there. There, there.

08:56.050 --> 08:57.550
Let's eat macarons together!

08:57.850 --> 08:58.160
Okay?

09:00.750 --> 09:02.860
Maybe it's starting to miss its friends.

09:03.300 --> 09:04.800
Homesickness, is it not?

09:05.150 --> 09:07.190
We'll take you back to your friends in no time, promise.

09:07.620 --> 09:09.150
So let's hang in there and do our best for a bit longer, okay?

09:09.600 --> 09:12.970
You've got to eat this and recover your strength so you can go back to your friends!

09:15.950 --> 09:17.870
I'm so glad it likes them.

09:18.100 --> 09:19.400
Let's set off once we're done.

09:20.790 --> 09:22.220
Oh, it's an Erikiteru!

09:24.010 --> 09:25.590
This guy's called an "Erikiteru".

09:37.250 --> 09:38.010
It's safe.

09:38.470 --> 09:40.520
This Erikiteru is our friend!

09:42.240 --> 09:43.930
There, there. It's true!

09:50.020 --> 09:52.530
See? Everything's fine, Bokurei.

09:55.370 --> 09:57.290
Thank goodness, it looks like it's come out of its shell.

10:06.970 --> 10:09.350
It seems to have become used to other Pokémon as well.

10:09.950 --> 10:10.240
Right?

10:10.580 --> 10:11.880
There's nothing to be scared about.

10:12.220 --> 10:14.160
Let's make a lot more friends!

10:16.920 --> 10:20.760
Are the brats trying to return that Bokurei to its habitat?

10:21.140 --> 10:23.480
That guy's Forest's Curse is bothersome.

10:23.730 --> 10:25.510
And it'll hinder us from getting Pikachu, too.

10:25.900 --> 10:27.280
We need to separate them.

10:27.560 --> 10:29.690
But what should we do?

10:29.850 --> 10:31.210
Isn't that obvious?

10:31.900 --> 10:33.540
This is where we take them on with our acting skills!

10:33.910 --> 10:34.570
Huh?

10:34.980 --> 10:35.850
Acting skills?

10:37.850 --> 10:40.420
Once we manage to separate Bokurei from them with our realistic acting,

10:41.050 --> 10:43.010
we'll finally get Pikachu today!

10:49.850 --> 10:50.700
Pokémon Quiz.

10:51.130 --> 10:51.890
The answer is...?

10:54.600 --> 10:56.770
The Pokémon Elections 720!

10:57.650 --> 11:01.290
Push the d-button on your remote control and vote for the Pokémon you want!

11:02.040 --> 11:11.970
Coming up next:

11:02.040 --> 11:07.010
Bokurei's friends have appeared!

11:03.030 --> 11:07.700
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

11:07.040 --> 11:11.970
But something's off...?

11:18.920 --> 11:21.630
It'd be great if we could make many more friends, huh?

11:24.460 --> 11:25.940
Kir, kir!

11:26.620 --> 11:27.500
Oh, look!

11:28.080 --> 11:28.880
It's a Kirlia!

11:29.110 --> 11:30.730
There's an Ellade and a Sirknight too!

11:30.910 --> 11:32.260
And even a Ralts!

11:32.890 --> 11:33.800
Amazing!

11:34.540 --> 11:37.810
The entire quartet is complete, evolved forms and all!

11:38.450 --> 11:39.300
El, el!

11:40.040 --> 11:43.240
Attract Bokurei's attention, lead it away and then abandon it wherever it seems fit.

11:43.730 --> 11:44.150
Got it?

11:44.440 --> 11:45.840
Make sure your acting's on point.

11:46.160 --> 11:46.730
Okay!

11:47.090 --> 11:47.770
Leave it to us.

11:48.050 --> 11:48.980
Understood.

11:50.880 --> 11:52.460
Kir, kir.

11:58.010 --> 12:00.040
Kir, kir!

12:00.410 --> 12:01.860
They're having a good time playing together.

12:02.470 --> 12:03.690
I'm so glad for you, Bokurei.

12:06.630 --> 12:07.030
Now!

12:07.290 --> 12:08.050
Roger!

12:12.610 --> 12:13.390
Let's follow them!

12:15.070 --> 12:16.600
Ah, please wait!

12:20.360 --> 12:21.620
Wait!

12:23.000 --> 12:25.620
What? Now the brats are following us too!

12:26.920 --> 12:29.420
This is bad. At this rate, they're going to catch up.

12:29.770 --> 12:30.910
Speed up!

12:40.160 --> 12:41.670
Whoa!

12:40.570 --> 12:41.430
Bokurei!

12:42.040 --> 12:43.510
Eureka will catch it!

12:44.160 --> 12:44.620
Huh?

12:44.880 --> 12:46.020
Where are Kirlia and the others?

12:51.580 --> 12:53.890
Could they have gone off somewhere?

12:53.890 --> 12:54.970
Aw...

12:55.270 --> 12:57.760
Eureka wanted to play with them too...

13:09.280 --> 13:11.260
This time, our scenario is perfect.

13:12.020 --> 13:14.440
You have to put on a perfect act, got it?

13:14.830 --> 13:16.800
What? You wanna continue?

13:17.050 --> 13:17.570
Of course.

13:18.080 --> 13:19.580
I'm counting on you!

13:28.080 --> 13:29.370
Hm? Those are Bokurei.

13:31.650 --> 13:32.890
Borei! Borei!

13:33.130 --> 13:33.600
Borei, borei!

13:37.740 --> 13:38.730
Are they its friends?

13:38.990 --> 13:40.410
Are they here to pick it up?

13:40.650 --> 13:41.540
I'm sure they are.

13:42.000 --> 13:42.890
They must've been looking for it!

13:43.480 --> 13:44.650
Borei, borei!

13:48.510 --> 13:49.990
They seem to be telling it to come closer.

13:50.650 --> 13:51.230
Let's go.

13:51.720 --> 13:52.130
Yeah.

13:56.100 --> 13:57.750
Borei, borei!

13:58.250 --> 13:59.240
Borei!

14:00.090 --> 14:00.380
Borei...

14:00.380 --> 14:01.040
Wait!

14:01.690 --> 14:03.050
Looks like they were successful.

14:05.690 --> 14:07.990
Now it's finally my turn.

14:15.250 --> 14:15.580
Huh?

14:16.650 --> 14:19.010
Borei, borei, borei!

14:19.210 --> 14:21.020
Borei!

14:21.620 --> 14:22.810
Oh, over there!

14:25.230 --> 14:28.380
H-Hey... Wait...!

14:28.570 --> 14:31.030
Geez! Pull yourself together, bro!

14:32.790 --> 14:34.120
Satoshi?

14:36.050 --> 14:36.540
Uh... Huh?

14:37.950 --> 14:39.280
This is my macaron.

14:39.610 --> 14:40.510
But why...?

14:42.310 --> 14:44.780
I wonder if Musashi was successful too.

14:46.390 --> 14:47.830
Geez, this is tiring...

14:49.450 --> 14:51.230
Sorry that we're not your friends.

14:53.140 --> 14:53.840
The Rocket Gang!

14:54.140 --> 14:55.250
Gulp!

14:55.250 --> 14:56.240
What are you doing here?

14:56.440 --> 14:57.550
They've found us!

14:58.120 --> 15:00.080
H-How did you find this place?

15:00.390 --> 15:02.300
Bokurei dropped a macaron.

15:02.520 --> 15:05.210
And it's weird for it to be dropping macarons when it loves them!

15:05.210 --> 15:06.910
Please return Bokurei!

15:07.920 --> 15:10.080
Geez, what's Musashi doing?!

15:10.810 --> 15:15.110
Anyway, as we'd planned, it's time for this bothersome Bokurei to make its leave!

15:18.810 --> 15:19.790
Here goes!

15:25.060 --> 15:26.190
It worked out!

15:26.190 --> 15:26.800
We're going home!

15:28.450 --> 15:29.650
I can't believe these people!

15:30.000 --> 15:30.750
Bokurei!

15:30.750 --> 15:32.200
Serena, let us go.

15:32.490 --> 15:32.820
Yeah.

15:35.880 --> 15:36.250
Those are...

15:48.590 --> 15:49.360
Amazing!

15:49.610 --> 15:51.030
Is it its real friends this time?

15:54.490 --> 15:56.340
Bokurei, are you hurt?

15:58.860 --> 16:00.750
Bokurei, are they all your friends?

16:02.710 --> 16:05.340
You've come all the way here to look for Bokurei, right?

16:11.370 --> 16:13.230
Borei, borei, borei!

16:12.720 --> 16:13.230
Hey!

16:13.230 --> 16:14.230
Wait up!

16:17.050 --> 16:18.300
Kurei!

16:20.570 --> 16:21.000
Kurei!

16:21.640 --> 16:22.190
Kurei!

16:22.890 --> 16:23.470
Kurei!

16:24.500 --> 16:25.180
What's going on?!

16:27.140 --> 16:29.620
If you ask us "What's going on? Pikapi!",

16:30.190 --> 16:32.090
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

16:32.690 --> 16:34.690
To prevent the world's destruction!

16:35.050 --> 16:37.110
To protect the world's peace!

16:37.620 --> 16:40.140
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

16:40.700 --> 16:42.700
we're lovely, charmy villains!

16:44.180 --> 16:44.760
Musashi!

16:45.170 --> 16:45.740
Kojiro!

16:46.120 --> 16:48.880
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

16:49.130 --> 16:51.740
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

16:52.060 --> 16:53.490
Just kidding!

16:57.540 --> 16:58.460
Rocket Gang!

17:00.190 --> 17:03.470
Operation: Bokurei Impersonation was a brilliant success!

17:04.090 --> 17:08.430
As I'm a great actress, I hope you were satisfied with my realistic acting.

17:08.800 --> 17:10.190
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

17:13.870 --> 17:15.160
It's no use!

17:15.160 --> 17:19.280
We made sure neither a Thunderbolt nor an entire Thunderstorm could penetrate this!

17:19.530 --> 17:20.650
And that's that!

17:22.330 --> 17:22.840
Ha!

17:23.190 --> 17:23.720
Wait!

17:28.560 --> 17:29.730
Pikachu!

17:33.890 --> 17:36.070
What the heck? Stop making strange voices!

17:36.550 --> 17:38.050
No, no! It's not me.

17:38.350 --> 17:40.170
Aren't these voices...?

17:41.140 --> 17:43.050
I knew it was the Bokurei!

17:43.260 --> 17:44.260
What?!

17:44.690 --> 17:45.270
What?

17:45.530 --> 17:46.330
Satoshi!

17:47.450 --> 17:50.030
Bokurei's friends have come to pick it up!

17:50.920 --> 17:51.810
I see!

18:03.660 --> 18:04.330
Pikachu!

18:05.490 --> 18:06.710
I'm so glad you're safe!

18:09.660 --> 18:11.970
Now you've done it!

18:14.520 --> 18:20.980
What? They're saying, "You ate our offerings without warning, didn't even apologize, and put our friend through a lot trouble on top of that!"

18:20.980 --> 18:23.510
"We won't forgive you for this!"

18:24.040 --> 18:25.940
I really can't believe you guys!

18:27.920 --> 18:31.450
There were so many! Sharing a bit wouldn't hurt, cheapskates!

18:31.930 --> 18:34.160
Pumpjin, use Dark Pulse to blast them away!

18:34.640 --> 18:36.810
Maaiika, Psybeam!

18:47.050 --> 18:47.740
What?!

18:48.210 --> 18:49.740
Good job, Bokurei!

19:00.710 --> 19:02.220
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

19:09.660 --> 19:11.280
This feels bad!

19:15.740 --> 19:17.350
All right, all right!

19:19.030 --> 19:19.710
Yay!

19:26.470 --> 19:27.750
Feel free to eat these together.

19:28.190 --> 19:28.970
Have this too.

19:36.290 --> 19:37.810
Bokurei, take care.

19:38.370 --> 19:39.950
Don't get lost again, okay?

19:57.760 --> 20:00.140
Oh, you want to introduce your friends right away?

20:01.810 --> 20:03.850
Make sure to make a lot more friends!

20:07.370 --> 20:09.650
See you! Everyone, take care!

20:11.310 --> 20:12.420
Bye-bye!

20:13.210 --> 20:17.930
The alternate-colored Bokurei managed to reunite with its friends and safely return to its habitat.

20:18.870 --> 20:23.100
And so, Satoshi and his friends once again set off towards Eisetsu City.

20:28.920 --> 20:31.250
Ugh... I'm hungry...

20:31.250 --> 20:34.140
Isn't there anything tasty lying around here...?

20:38.110 --> 20:39.140
Th-These voices...!

20:41.760 --> 20:43.610
L-Let's run!

20:46.150 --> 20:47.130
For real?

20:47.130 --> 20:48.600
Yeah, I'm telling you!

20:54.310 --> 20:57.010
Special info on the Pokémon movie!

20:57.710 --> 21:00.420
We meet the ingenious Pokémon Magearna.

21:00.720 --> 21:01.830
This is amazing!

21:01.830 --> 21:05.110
The Pokémon of miracles... If I can get my hands on that...

21:05.820 --> 21:10.720
The lovely Magearna is actually hiding power so great it could change the world!

21:11.910 --> 21:17.580
On sale until Friday July 15th

21:12.320 --> 21:13.910
This movie can be enjoyed with...

21:13.910 --> 21:17.500
...a special pre-order ticket that comes with a giveaway code for Volcanion!

21:17.750 --> 21:20.840
Premieres Saturday July 16th!

21:17.850 --> 21:20.080
Everyone, please make sure to get one!

21:20.920 --> 21:25.910
Pokémon no Uchi Atsumaru?

21:20.920 --> 21:25.910
Sunday May 1st at 8am

21:21.660 --> 21:22.820
Pippi!

21:23.330 --> 21:25.160
Pokénchi airs Sundays at 8am!

21:28.260 --> 21:30.160
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.350 --> 21:31.440
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.750 --> 21:35.540
You're Carne-san, the Champion of the Kalos region!

21:35.750 --> 21:39.030
Satoshi-kun, has there been any strange incidents happening around you and your friends?

21:39.510 --> 21:42.040
Just that my Gekkouga powered up, I think...

21:42.400 --> 21:44.460
Satoshi-kun, have a battle with me!

